        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12424953/comment/12708135",
          "id": "12708135",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=pkd",
            "name": "pkd",
            "key": "pkd",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Peter Dettman",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "You're welcome... unfortunately the previous patch was not quite right. The GarbageCollector needs to keep a reference to the session listener or it may be garbage collected (the session only holds weak references to its listeners). I observed this actually occurring in testing on the latest build.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=pkd",
            "name": "pkd",
            "key": "pkd",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Peter Dettman",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-11T17:55:25.070+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-11T17:55:25.070+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12424953/comment/12708136",
          "id": "12708136",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=pkd",
            "name": "pkd",
            "key": "pkd",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Peter Dettman",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Patch against latest build (on top of previous patch). Stores the session listener in a field of GarbageCollector so that it is not collected.\n\nAlso moves the closing of the system sessions from loggedOut() to loggingOut(); it seems more appropriate that the lifetime of those system sessions be bounded by the parent session.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=pkd",
            "name": "pkd",
            "key": "pkd",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Peter Dettman",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-11T17:59:42.850+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-11T17:59:42.850+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12424953/comment/12708452",
          "id": "12708452",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=thomasm",
            "name": "thomasm",
            "key": "tmueller",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Thomas Mueller",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "Hm, the GarbageCollector object could be garbage collected before the session is closed.\nThat means keeping a hard reference from the GarbageCollector to the listener\nwouldn't help, right?\n\nIt looks like we need a new method GarbageCollector.close(), and a finalize() method\n(in case people forgot to call close()).",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=thomasm",
            "name": "thomasm",
            "key": "tmueller",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Thomas Mueller",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-12T14:47:41.875+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-12T14:47:41.875+0000"
        },
        {
